By this reasoning universities could ban gay student groups for fear
that they would say something the university disagrees with.

In fact, most private universities make a contractual promise to their
students that the students shall be free of "institutional censorship"
even in university-owned forums. Not only does this promote free
expression (thought by many to be important to university's mission),
but it also gets the university off the hook for what the students
say. The courts generally say that as long as the university doesn't
control what the students say then the university is not legally
responsible for it.

