country, to speak (freely and loudly) for your rights, both equal and in
fact for those which are in excess of what majority people have, and to
attempt to educate others about the merits of your lifestyle.

As a member of a minority group myself, I AM <extremely> sensitive to
attempts to silence those who have dissenting opinions.

Unlike you, however, I apply the same standards of conduct to my own
actions that I proffer towards others, and even though I may disagree wiht
someone's message, I refuse to get involved in attempts to prevent it from
being communicated as long as it remains within legal boundaries.

