While such searches may be legal at private universities (it depends
on the Student Code), I believe they are highly unethical. 

Also, remember even though your university does own the computers, the
sys admin doesn't. Does your university really trust a sys admin to,
on his or her own, search the computer files of professors and
supervisors? Does it trust him or her to understand and comply with
the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act and the Electronic
Commincations Privacy Act?  For state universities, can he or he be
trusted to understand the 5th Amendment rights of students and staff?

Here at U. of Illinois there was enough outrage when a department
claimed authority to conduct arbitrary searches that the University
now explicitly forbids arbitrary searches.

