                Looking for a Social Architectress?

     Now that I have graduated from school with the highest degree
the state has to offer, one would think there would be plenty of
jobs available for doctresses of education.  One might ask, "Isn't
the educational system in crisis?  Don't we need thinkers who are
thinking a way out of the problems?  Aren't we in desperate need of
futurists who are working to create a new curriculum which
liberates the new technologies?  Since the Cold War is over, isn't
this the time for peace educators to give us a new Vision of a
peaceful use of Cyberspace?  Isn't it time to institute an ideology
of true love so that we can begin feeding all the world's people?
Isn't there a job out there for Doctress Neutopia?" 

     These are questions that seemed to be ignored by the powers
who control our lives.  The purpose of post-modern indoctrination
oh, excuse me, I should say education is to maintain the
patriarchal status quo.  Of course, this means that there should be
as little, if any, futurist talk because true futurism leads us to
question the values of the ruling class, the billionaires and their
companions since they are the one's who have the power to carry out
their intention to shape the future.  Even an idiot can figure out
that it is just not fair for a few individuals to have billions of
dollars and more than one luxury home while others are living in
poverty on the streets.  The realization that we are living in a
state of vast social inequality is bound to lead us to a social
lovolution.  If students really started comprehending ideas of
social justice and questioning authority, how could they
consciously go on supporting the status quo?  Such thoughts could
even pull them away from the TV sets and the Rose Bowl games to get
them to organize Neutopian learning webs in order to change the
unjust virtual reality for the future of the human race. 

     Oh, yes, back to my job hunt.  Well, I have just explored a
few of the reasons why the Clinton Administration has not proposed
a revolutionary agenda in education since it would threaten the
entire existence of free-market capitalism.  Instead, he has opted
for educational reform where math and science lead the way,
disciplines which have traditionally excluded women. He believes
this is the means through which America will be competitive in the
global economy and remain the number one superpower.  But there is
no way around the crying need for an educational revolution.  More
state police and more guns in the hands of the authorities pointed
at students so that they will continue to sit quietly in their
chairs as good all-American citizens is simply not going to stop
violence because it has not addressed the ignorance which caused
it. 

     If he was really serious about preparing students for the 21st
Century so that they will be able to exercise their rights in a
spiritual democracy, he would have a completely different approach
to education. He would be opening people up to the world growing in
Cyberspace where everyone is working in cooperation to create
arcologies of peace and true love.  This means we need a corps of
instructors who can teach the basic email skills necessary for life
in a spiritual democracy.  These teachers must be visionaries who
can lead us into the world of Neutopian Thought.

     Back to the job market.  There are several places where one
can go in Usenet to search for jobs.  One such place on Usenet is
labeled misc.jobs.  One night when I went through the list in hopes
of finding a job, I found 1,000 or so job listings.  It didn't take
me long for it to become clear to me that we are living in a
technocracy.  In a technocracy, the technocrats as members of the
big boy's club, get the jobs, those students who excelled in math
and science, a dominate patriarchal section of the job world has
the inside track.  There are abating number of jobs for computer
programmers and computer analysts, and/or computer scientists
researchers who are building the physical structures of the new
world.  These are lucrative jobs, not your nine to five, minimum
wage slave jobs which kill one's creative desire.

     I only saw one job listed that was looking for an educator. 
A man was looking for a nanny for his two sons.  For me to become
a private nanny seems like a waste of my life.  My role is to do
teacher education, to teach teachers about my Neutopian philosophy
of planetary liberation.  I am a change artist, a social
architectress, a conceptional artist who sees a grand vision for
Clinton/Gore's information highway.  But, I can see where their
information highway should end.  It is a superhighway to a wondrous
network of arcologies on Earth and in Outerspace. The superhighway
leads us to a new kind of university, a Neutopian transversity
where the computer assists us in individual education so that each
of us will be enabled to live out our own noble dreams.

     I would like to remind President Clinton that the only way to
end violence around the world is through creativity.  Doesn't he
know that basically the schools, both the public and the private,
are crushing the potential of the minds of the youth, making them
into petty robots whose major concern in life is who is wearing
designer clothes?  So, what we need is a revolution of creativity.
I can see it now like in the 1930's WPA Hallie Flanagon:  jobs in
creative anthropology and sociology, jobs in creative writing, jobs
in comparative literature, jobs in art education, jobs for
actresses and actors, jobs for revolutionary playwrights, jobs in
the visual arts, jobs in poetry, jobs in dance, job in music and
yes there is a job for me as a social architectress. And I am
having a great time drawing the blueprints for a Neutopian
Cyberworld.  After I am in my proper position and the culture-
makers are all working for the same cause of building Neutopia,
then the technocrats can work for the beauty of creating an
entirely different kind of world, a world where Wisdom rules and
everyone has the resources to allow their gifts and talents to
grow.

     Of all the millions of jobs President Clinton has promised us
he would create, how many do you think are for change artists or
for a social architectress?  How many are for revolutionary
educators?  It is as if the politicians and technocrats think they
don't need revolutionary art.  They can have an "information
revolution" without the change artists because in their mind, they
don't really want to change the culture.  They just want it so that
the rich make even more money by exploiting the poor.  They think
junk popular entertainment is fine to digest when they get back
from their high-paying corporate jobs.  Hell, that is all they have
ever been fed in their lives, so why should they want anything
different? The society has trained them to think anti-status quo
art is bad and it shouldn't be subsidize.  So what they do support
are things that they call practical for them while the things of
the spirit are denied.

     With our advanced technologies we have the means to create a
leisure based economy or one in which everyone does work for a few
hours a day.  Only then will we have a true democracy because
democracy requires people to have the time necessary to be able to
learn about the controversial issues which are being discussed and
faces us constantly.  Now, even students are to busy with school
work to even think about the issues being debated.  And workers are
too tired at night to really learn about issues that are not
covered on the TV news.  They have been shuffling meaningless,
bureaucratic papers all day, so why would they want to come home
and open up a book?  Do you think the ruling class wants to create
a leisure class of ordinary citizens who with more time on their
hands to contemplate the injustices of the world might come to the
conclusion that the only way out of our damned predicament is to
erase class differences?

     I remember an anthropologist professor telling me that in the
1960's when the students went on strike, the leisure time allowed
several of his students to really contemplate issues and write
profound papers on social topics.  He said that he had never
received such thoughtful papers before or since the student strike.

The Establishment knows how and has the means through the media to
keep the masses loyal to the good old Protestant ethic.  For
Clinton, a good citizen is a workaholic who doesn't even mind doing
shit work for five dollars an hour. But if she or he needs to see
a lawyer in a labor dispute, out of their five dollars an hour she
or he has to pay 80 dollars an hour to a lawyer for legal advice
only to find out that there is no justice in the American judicial
system.  Once you are caught in the judicial system, there is no
way around it.  You are going to have to pay whether you win or
lose.  Isn't that the basic principle of paytriarchy, if you want
justice you have to pay, and pay, and pay and then not have
justice?

     The New World of Neutopian Thought is a leisure economy.  We
support individual attempts at creating mistress and master pieces
in both the arts and sciences.  This is a world where people take
pride in whatever work they do knowing that they are contributing
to the good of the whole.  In Neutopia, mediocrity is not the norm
as everyone strives for the Ideal Ecocity. Doing work for money is
a thought only associated with slavery. Neutopians are intelligent
enough to know that justice is not about life, liberty, and the
pursuit of property.  They realize that the accumulation of power,
property, and clan survival is not the way to the happy world.

     So now, back to my job search.  As a doctress of education, I
know what my real work is...to be a teacher and a visionary artist,
standing against the forces of destruction which are killing the
global ecology.  I feel all my time should be spent on changing our
social reality so that creative people are free to do their own
work to save our delicate ecosystem.  Now, where am I going to find
allies, my support system?

     Isn't someone like me who is a social critic the prime
candidate for a tenure faculty position?  Think again, people.  The
educational system is the handmaiden of the political system.  Note
that the word faculty has the word "cult" in it.  Yes, the
educational system is a giant cult whose head is the President of
The USA.  Since I have ideas that oppose their visions or lack of
them, well, it becomes difficult to make it into the system.  They
only employ conformists who accept the rhetoric of nationalism and
those injustices that follow the dictates of the global
corporations.

     But we are going to change all this, right?  We are going to
make the Internet into a place where Neutopian Idealist can create
a new world where everyones gifts, talents, and skills are used,
loved, and cherished.  What other choice do Outsiders have but to
overthrow our present nightmare?  Only then will there we work and
leisure time for all.  Then justice will reign and Neutopia will
come into existence.













